{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493441-i-m-always-angry","id":493441,"title":"\"I'm always angry\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-27T04:41:39-07:00","id":493441,"title":"\"I'm always angry\"","content":"Maybe it's the fact that the sequel is only a few days away, or maybe it was blurb about belongings shifting with you on page 96, but a few mintues ago I found myself thinking about the Hulk in Avengers. Right up until the final battle scene, everyone was asking him what the secret to keeping the monster inside him under control was. It wasn't finding a calm place to live or yoga or pilates. So what was it? How did keep the beast down?<br /> The way he controlled it was by accepting it.<br /> That seems like a good picture of Harmony. Deny that you're both beast and man and things get out of control. Work torgether with the other guy, recognize that he's in there and important, and things go more smoothly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T05:17:44-07:00","id":493471,"title":"","content":"I teared up at that scene.<br /> <br /> Also, few days!? I'm going to see it today!<br /> <br /> And lastly, yeah, that's definitely how I see harmony. You're not fighting against your dual natures, but accepting each when they have needs or are relevant.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I think that the description of rage is a bit of misnomer for WWs though. I feel like it's more an embracing of their instinctive killing-ness. They're not really <i>angry</i> per se, but they are intent on killing everything the can see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T05:20:25-07:00","id":493475,"title":"","content":"That sounds like rage to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T07:12:58-07:00","id":493568,"title":"","content":"&quot;How do you not have any personal <i>kuruth</i> triggers?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm always hunting.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T07:32:30-07:00","id":493581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493441-i-m-always-angry#post493441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's the fact that the sequel is only a few days away, .</div> </div> </div> </div>It was realesed earlier in the movies here in Brazil(and some other parts of the world I think, but not the USA). Already watched it<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> About Hulk and Harmony analogy, don't know if Werewolf is the best one, I believe it's better to think the Hulk as a Geist, a second personality.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T08:14:37-07:00","id":493644,"title":"","content":"MCU Hulk is closer to a werewolf than the comic version. It's left up in the air how much he's a genuine alternate personality and how much he's just Banner with his adrenaline shot through the roof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T10:15:40-07:00","id":493723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493441-i-m-always-angry?p=493581#post493581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Hulk and Harmony analogy, don't know if Werewolf is the best one, I believe it's better to think the Hulk as a Geist, a second personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;So you're saying that the Hulk \u2014 the other guy \u2014 saved my life? That's a nice sentiment. Saved it for what?&quot;<br /> &quot;I guess we'll have to find out.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T10:30:43-07:00","id":493731,"title":"","content":"I think the movies gloss over way too much of the background to really know. The obvious similarity to werewolf is that he changes into a rampaging monster, but the Hulk isn't exactly a death raging gauru.<br /> <br /> In the comics the reasons for Banners' anger constantly shifts, blaming it on repressed homosexuality, memories of childhood abuse, other things, to the point that when he's separated from the Hulk he turns into a mad scientist hating his own, human weakness.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, someone like the Fire-Touched may appreciate being at low Harmony. They are more spirit-like, so they suffer the bans of spirits. At higher humanity, a person is very human, they just have an anger issue that comes up every once and awhile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-27-2015, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T10:45:18-07:00","id":493738,"title":"","content":"While it might be a bit incidental, the way I currently interpret that line isn't a matter of acceptance so much as being able to keep the transformation under wraps by being in a constant state of low-level aggression (and passive aggression, such as the degree to which he snarks about things that might violently set him off) to reduce incidents of sudden sharp bursts.<br /> <br /> It's like, I look back at that film and feel as though he's really playing it as Banner constantly being on edge. If he's always angry, then it becomes a default and a mundanity to him except for occasions where he actually wants to let people see how he's really feeling (or when a violent physical shock breaks down his barriers for a bit).<br /> <br /> It's interesting, but I don't exactly see the way they were playing Banner in that movie to be especially uplifting.<br /> <br /> Does that relate to Werewolf? .... Possibly. Thinking on it, I would say I don't exactly see the Second Edition version of Harmony as being in a state of acceptance so much as constantly maintained equilibrium between irreconcilable extremes compelled by ever present impulses. And it's like... the only way to keep it stable is to kind of immerse yourself in the circumstances of it, which is a bit different from acceptance.<br /> <br /> The Uratha are cool and all, but I wouldn't want to personally be one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T11:19:13-07:00","id":493760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493441-i-m-always-angry?p=493738#post493738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Uratha are cool and all, but I wouldn't want to personally be one.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that can be said about any of the nWOD splats...<br /> <br /> Vampires are cool and all, but I wouldn't want to be one...<br /> Mages are cool and all, but I wouldn't want to be one...<br /> Changelings are cool and all, but I wouldn't want to be one...<br /> <br /> Etc. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T11:25:55-07:00","id":493764,"title":"","content":"Mages and Sin-Eaters have little in the way of drawbacks for the obscene power they get. Provided you're not casting vulgar magic you should be fine.<br /> <br /> I'd be more willing to make a jump to Uratha once we get a more definitive say about their lifespan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T11:41:07-07:00","id":493769,"title":"","content":"Being a mage is pretty good most of the time, but when it turns ugly it does so abruptly and with extreme prejudice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T12:05:21-07:00","id":493822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493441-i-m-always-angry?p=493738#post493738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it might be a bit incidental, the way I currently interpret that line isn't a matter of acceptance so much as being able to keep the transformation under wraps by being in a constant state of low-level aggression... <br /> <br /> Does that relate to Werewolf? .... Possibly. Thinking on it, I would say I don't exactly see the Second Edition version of Harmony as being in a state of acceptance so much as constantly maintained equilibrium between irreconcilable extremes compelled by ever present impulses. And it's like... the only way to keep it stable is to kind of immerse yourself in the circumstances of it, which is a bit different from acceptance.<br /> <br /> The Uratha are cool and all, but I wouldn't want to personally be one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting it that way, they still kinda sound like the same thing. Maybe that thing shouldn't be classified as &quot;acceptance&quot;, but they ring similar.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I don't think it'd want to be a Uratha, either. I like pretending, though. As my wife puts it &quot;it's being reminded that there are dark and scary things out there, but being able to remember at the same time that I'm scarier still.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Mage, however, is a different story altogether...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T13:15:01-07:00","id":493900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493441-i-m-always-angry?p=493760#post493760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that can be said about any of the nWOD splats...<br /> <br /> Vampires are cool and all, but I wouldn't want to be one...<br /> Mages are cool and all, but I wouldn't want to be one...<br /> Changelings are cool and all, but I wouldn't want to be one...<br /> <br /> Etc. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Speak for yourself! If there's a shot at immortality, I am down. Side effects be damned","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T02:18:53-07:00","id":494528,"title":"","content":"On the topic of being a splat, I'd chose demon and simply observe through the centuries (so analyst Inquisitor I guess)<br /> <br /> On topic: So the hulk is just a hairless werewolf? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T04:12:17-07:00","id":494579,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4046/4379565437_ac8d2b932a.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:05:52-07:00","id":494737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493441-i-m-always-angry?p=493764#post493764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages and Sin-Eaters have little in the way of drawbacks for the obscene power they get. Provided you're not casting vulgar magic you should be fine.<br /> <br /> I'd be more willing to make a jump to Uratha once we get a more definitive say about their lifespan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sin-Eaters have a dead crazed death demi-god stuck in their head.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, Dem Bones is a clear cut case of why it <i>sucks</i> to be a Sin-Eater sometimes.<br /> <br /> As for Mages, oh, yeah, sure. If I'm not careful with what I do, I may implode. My power has serious consequences if I don't know what I'm doing with it.<br /> <br /> THat's not very thrilling for a lackadaisical person like myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:13:08-07:00","id":494755,"title":"","content":"Death by paradox seems like something that would only happen in the most specifically planned of circumstances or if you were already on the verge of death.<br /> <br /> As for a geist 'living' with you, considering the limited immortality and vast power, it may be worth the price, especially considering the base wants of the geister. Regan's geist is a unique one and her own way of dealing with it, suicide, is also uncommon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-28-2015, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:19:20-07:00","id":494758,"title":"","content":"I think the most likely form paradox-related death takes is getting your face chewed off by an abyssal entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:25:41-07:00","id":494764,"title":"","content":"Yes, but it takes 4-5 Arcanum dots in your spell to have something that dangerous, and 5 or more successes on a paradox dicepool to even have a chance of it happening, something you can't even get without around 5 Gnosis and even then you have to be casting a vulgar spell in front of sleepers or repeatedly invoking paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-28-2015, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:00:55-07:00","id":494829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493441-i-m-always-angry?p=494755#post494755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death by paradox seems like something that would only happen in the most specifically planned of circumstances or if you were already on the verge of death.<br /> <br /> As for a geist 'living' with you, considering the limited immortality and vast power, it may be worth the price, especially considering the base wants of the geister. Regan's geist is a unique one and her own way of dealing with it, suicide, is also uncommon.</div> </div> </div> </div>1)That's the sort of thinking that gets you killed.<br /> 2) There's still a hell of a cautionary tale in there<br /> <br /> Dem bones, dem bones, dem bones are gonna walk all over, dem bones, dem bones, dem bones are gonna walk all over, dem bones, dem bones, dem bones are gonna walk all over, dem bones, dem bones, dem bones are gonna walk all over, dem bones, dem bones, dem bones are gonna walk all over, dem bones, dem bones, dem bones are gonna walk all over, dem bones, dem bones, dem bones are gonna walk all over, dem bones, dem bones, dem bones are gonna walk all over...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T11:05:48-07:00","id":495025,"title":"","content":"But what if a Mage died of paradox and then came back as a Sin-Eater? What Threshold would that be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T11:13:53-07:00","id":495044,"title":"","content":"Probably the Suicide one, if you 'soaked' the damage from it. Accident if by a slim chance your slight paradox manages to kill you. The killed by others one if you manage to summon an entity that wants to kill you and it manages to do so. <br /> <br /> I forget the names of them all, apologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-28-2015, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T11:19:52-07:00","id":495047,"title":"","content":"I'd say death by chance but that might be a bit too meta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T11:44:34-07:00","id":495059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanandithras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493441-i-m-always-angry?p=494579#post494579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4046/4379565437_ac8d2b932a.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, not hairless werewolf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T12:32:34-07:00","id":495089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493441-i-m-always-angry?p=495025#post495025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what if a Mage died of paradox and then came back as a Sin-Eater? What Threshold would that be?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an intereting one. I don't know if its strictly forbidden, either, since a dead Mage is typically just a dead Mage.<br /> <br /> I don't think Stricken would fit, unless the Mage in question really thought of paradox as a disease of the supernal.<br /> As nofather said, Silent could work if the paradox-driven death was intentional.<br /> He could come back as one of the Prey if paradox seems to him like a dangerous natural concequence of channeling supernal energies.<br /> Torn seems unlikely as it's not an emotion-fueled murder.<br /> The Forgotten seems the most likely to me, from the outside player perspective. Getting killed by a Paradox is a pretty rough random chance. But it's not about the player perspective. It's about the perspective of the person who died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T13:10:36-07:00","id":495114,"title":"","content":"I would have to agree that Banner's whole schtick in the MCU is more like getting triggered into Kuruth if we're talking Werewolf, seems to be down to his adrenaline mainly. That he let go at the end of the 1st Avengers and stopped keeping himself calm, seemed a little off to me, but eh. That he triggered when he was injured on the Helicarrier and he was hyperventilating from the pain making the Hulk came out was really clever.<br /> Therein though the Hulk seems to have himself a unique Kuruth trigger and probably has an extremely high Harmony for a passive trigger based around his adrenaline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}